Apple today released minor iOS 26.4.2 and iPadOS 26.4.2 software updates for the iPhone and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a>, respectively. The updates are available two weeks after Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/08/apple-releases-ios-26-4-1/">released iOS 26.4.1 and iPadOS 26.4.1</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/04/iOS-26.4.2-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1045477" /><br/>
The new software can be downloaded on eligible iPhones and iPads over-the-air by going to Settings → General → Software Update.<br/>
<br/>
According to Apple's release notes, the software updates contain unspecified bug fixes and security updates. <br/>
<br/>
Apple also released iOS 18.7.8 for older iPhones that are not updated to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-26/">iOS 26</a>. <br/>
<br/>
